  "body": "## What changed\n- **One WCS per setup.** `SetupDef.wcs` is now one entity name (was a six-slot list); `SetupDef.work_offset` is only the `G54`..`G59` word the post writes for it. Relabelling moves no origin and no height. `setup::wcs_entity` / `wcs_entity_name` take no slot; new `setup::wcs_label` (\"WCS (G55)\").\n- **Commands.** `SetWcsOrigin::new(world, location)` places the active setup's one WCS (slot argument removed). A new setup's WCS is `<setup>/WCS`; the materialized first setup keeps pointing at the legacy `G54` entity (nothing renamed). Datum transfer clones the one WCS; DeleteSetup takes its own WCS with it.\n- **Browser.** The Setup section shows a single row labelled plain **WCS** (the posted word as its faint suffix). The G55-G59 / \"not placed\" rows are gone. Clicking it opens the WCS page (`UiTarget::Wcs`), which edits the active setup's origin through the undoable `SetWcs` (numeric origin, turns, anchors, vertex/face origin chips, 3-2-1 align, Origin ribbon cell). The Setups-page dropdown is the only place the word is chosen.\n- **Wording.** The WCS page heading, setup sheet (`WCS` section, `WCS (G55)` line), rotated-WCS refusal, Heights page read-only row, viewport height chip (`(WCS G55 +25.00)`), status lines and MCP `get_job` (`wcs` is now one object: label/word/placed/entity/origin/rotation) all speak of the setup's WCS.\n\n## Migration (project v54, `project::wcs_one`)\n- Each v53 setup keeps the entity (name and placement) of the slot it posted (its pick, else G54) as its one WCS, so single-WCS documents post byte for byte.\n- Placed slots that no setup posted are dropped, each with a **load note** naming the entity and where it sat. `project::open_noted` / `load_noted` return the notes, the shell shows them in the status line, and they are logged.\n- A document without setups keeps `G54` as its WCS and drops the rest with notes.\n- An operation naming a setup the file does not hold posted at `<setup>/G54`. That entity is renamed `<setup>/WCS`, so the operation keeps its zero.\n- Two origins inside one setup only arise from v51-or-older files. The existing v52 rung refuses those by name before this rung runs, so the migration never picks an origin. A v54 file that still lists slots is refused as corrupt. A malformed old offset row is still refused by the validator, not dropped.\n- The two-setups-same-word-different-origin post refusal (#196) is unchanged.\n- Stamp shape unchanged (the work-offset word is still digested), so migrated stamps stay fresh. Relabelling therefore asks a work-offset-height op for one regenerate, which produces the same path.\n\n## Readings and tests\n- New `crates/app/tests/one_wcs.rs` (7):\n  - single placed slot posts identically;\n  - several placed slots keep the posted one and drop the rest with notes;\n  - a no-setup document keeps G54 and drops G55, and resaves byte-identical;\n  - two setups keep their own posted origins;\n  - an operation in a missing setup keeps its zero;\n  - v54 with a slot list is corrupt;\n  - a WCS edit undoes inside its own setup and a relabel spawns no origin.\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/one_wcs.rs` (2): the browser shows one WCS per setup with no slot rows, and the WCS row edits the active setup's origin undoably.\n- Rewritten for the new model: `setup_wcs` (relabel = word only, placing moves coordinates, undo), `setup_defines_wcs` (v51 fixtures built as JSON; conflicting v51 setups still refused by name), plus setups, heights, lathe_spindle_law, commands_undo, posting, rotated_wcs, project_roundtrip, setup_align and the ui shell/law/chip tests.\n- Shell snapshots regenerated (`egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png`). I checked them: the six G5x rows became one `WCS G54` row, and the chip reads `(WCS G54 +0.00)`.\n- Gate results:\n  - Passed (debug): app setup_wcs, setup_defines_wcs, one_wcs, rotated_wcs, wcs_align, setups, setup_sheet, setup_align, posting, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, heights, machine, lathe_spindle_law, golden_cl, conformance, fanuc_post, mcp, face_origin, drilling_cross_spindle/stock, lathe_field_sim, rotary_verify, operations, post_not_judged, heidenhain_block_form.\n  - Passed: all camcraft-ui suites run from `crates/ui` (lib 294 passed).\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n  - Failing, not caused by this PR: `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` asserts `PROJECT_VERSION == 51`. It already fails on main (53), and this bump makes it read 54.\n\nNot exercised: the GUI by hand. Decisions: `docs/decisions/342-one-wcs.md`.\n\nChangelog: One WCS per setup - the browser shows a single \"WCS\" node and G54-G59 is only the setup's post label; project v54 keeps each setup's posted origin and drops unposted slots with a load note (breaking: v54 files, SetWcsOrigin lost its slot) (#342)\n\nFixes #342\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
